  "name": "checking-member-access",
  "description": "Explains what a member or a role can do in a PostHog project, using the access control MCP tools. Use when the user asks what someone can see or edit, who can edit dashboards or feature flags, why a member can or cannot open a dashboard, notebook or table, what a role grants, which properties are hidden from someone, or how the project's default access is set. Covers what each level means, how the stored rule, the enforced level and the inherited access relate, what the null values mean, which tool answers which question, and when the answer needs the role tools too.",
